    {
      "title": "Hint",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 13 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**This dashboard reads from `nexus_slo:*` recording rules**, not raw histograms — so panels load fast and match the alert expressions exactly.\n\n**Per-panel meaning:**\n\n- **Top row stats**: current state vs SLO target. Background colour goes yellow at 75% of threshold, red at 100%. If a panel goes red, the corresponding Prometheus alert (e.g. `EventIngestP99LatencyBreached`) will be `pending` and will fire after `for: 5m`.\n\n- **Latency vs SLO thresholds**: trend over time. Watch for trajectories — a value approaching a threshold for 5 minutes is the multi-window alert pattern's design target.\n\n- **Error rate panel**: 5m and 1h series side-by-side. The fast/slow burn pattern from the SRE workbook is implemented as `ErrorBudgetFastBurn` (5m > 2%) and `ErrorBudgetSlowBurn` (1h > 0.5%). Both threshold lines are plotted.\n\n- **Latency by (method, path)**: drill-down for which route is slow. The Ch14 fix that swapped raw URL paths for chi route patterns means cardinality is bounded and PII-safe.\n\n- **Error budget gauge**: 100% = no errors consumed; 0% = budget exhausted; negative = over budget. Window is 7 days, not 30 (see `docs/SLOs.md` for why).\n\nRule definitions: `nexus/scripts/observability/recording-rules.yml`.\nSLO targets: `nexus/docs/SLOs.md`."
      }
    }
